BashKitten machine lifecycle and guest services

The external-rootfs Podman lifecycle, native guest sudo/PTY and AppImage FUSE
bridges, and separate-graph PipeWire/GStreamer media mechanisms derive from
Open Research Tools' BuzzardOS podman branch, commit
6c1b89f25c196ae7ab4a8f20e166b27e4ee94cc0.
Original source selection, full license, notices and source checksums are in
upstream/buzzard-runtime. Those retained components are AGPL-3.0-or-later.

Modified for BashKitten in October 2026: private stable user-data machine
storage; async Node controller and independent user-service lifetime; explicit
private Podman/helper paths; recoverable cleanup-before-unregister deletion;
rootful Xwayland/XFCE instead of Sway; guest BashKitten and private TLS Unix
handoff; passwordless guest policy; renamed guest paths; optional media bridges
owned by the environment rather than its viewer. No donor application shell,
separate product/updater or host-privilege command path is retained.

Original BashKitten modules are AGPL-3.0-only where so marked. Component license
texts and original copyright notices remain applicable; do not relabel donors.

Private libfuse 3.18.3 modification, 11 October 2026: require the configured
packaged fusermount3 path and report its spawn error without trying a host
installation. The named patch is retained under patches/libfuse; lib/mount.c
and this adaptation retain that file's GNU LGPLv2 terms. Original libfuse source
and full license texts remain in vendor/libfuse.

Guest FUSE integration, 18 October 2026: replace the AppImage-only Python mount
bridge with the unmodified native fusermount3 from the same pinned libfuse
3.18.3 source. The guest package installs it at a private path with guest-root
setuid ownership and diverts the distro command to a symlink, preserving normal
libfuse/AppImage/document-portal semantics. No host setuid helper or policy
change is installed. Its GPLv2 license and upstream notices are included in the
guest package; the pristine Buzzard bridge remains in upstream/buzzard-runtime.

Private Podman 6.1.3 modification, 11 October 2026: the rootless pause process
requires the configured packaged catatonit executable. It never searches the
host's catatonit paths or silently substitutes another pause implementation.
The named patch is retained under patches/podman and the private path is supplied
by the tracked build recipe. Original source and full Apache-2.0 notices remain
in vendor/podman; the modification retains those terms. Package provenance records
the patch checksum and build recipe checksum alongside the original release pin.

Release refresh, 19 October 2026: pristine Podman v6.1.4 at
464c15fec06f0074c916f9eff87c4806869c2833 replaces v6.1.3 with its complete
upstream vendored dependencies and full notices. The same private catatonit
patch applies without changes. crun 1.30.1 and the other private native helper
releases remain current. The sudo bridge's libc dependency is updated to
0.2.191, retaining its full MIT and Apache-2.0 texts and exact crate source.

Private netavark 2.1.0 and aardvark-dns 2.1.0 build metadata modifications,
11 October 2026: require each verified upstream release commit supplied by the
tracked recipe instead of discovering the enclosing build workspace's Git commit.
The named patches are retained under patches/netavark and patches/aardvark-dns.
Original source and full Apache-2.0 notices remain in their vendor directories;
the modifications retain those terms. Package provenance records both patch
checksums and the recipe checksum alongside the original release pins.
